FORWARDING NOTICE — this file is no longer the durable record.

The seL4 kernel change (ledger row 13 — split the trailing device-untyped region into a LOW+HIGH range so a high GOP framebuffer is covered) now lives IN the Genode
fork as a port patch file:

    genode/repos/base-sel4/patches/sel4-device-untyped-coverage.patch
    (fork: github.com/llaa33219/sponge-os-genode, `repos/base-sel4/patches/`)

`sel4.port` feeds `PATCHES := $(sort $(wildcard $(REP_DIR)/patches/*.patch))`
into `install.mk`, which applies each file with `patch -p0` during
`prepare_port sel4`. Nothing has to be applied by hand and nothing is
lost when `genode/contrib/` is re-fetched — that is precisely the
failure this move fixed (see docs/11-environment.md, "contrib re-fetch
incident").

To read or edit the change, open the fork file above. To see the diff
against a prepared tree:

    diff -u genode/contrib/sel4-*/<file> <(patch -R -o - -p0 < \
        genode/repos/base-sel4/patches/sel4-device-untyped-coverage.patch)

Drop condition: unchanged from ledger row 13.
